--- !u!114 &2651476017644967051
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7113765829624473140}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9541d86e2fd84c1d9990edf0852d74ab, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<i>After station 1.</i>\nBloom spreads the pixels brighter than its Threshold into their neighbours. The two halos have the same colour; one is 4 times brighter. In the HDR colour picker, Intensity counts in stops: each +1 doubles the value (value 1 = Intensity 0, value 4 = Intensity 2).\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Threshold 1. Which halo glows: value 1, value 4, or both?\n\n<b>Try:</b> Move the Threshold. Then untick HDR in the URP Asset (Quality \u203A HDR): what happens to the bloom? Tick it again. The camera has its own switch: Output \u203A HDR Rendering.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 02\u201304</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
